Subject: [PATCH] Restore work lost in df4290d; make CI green again
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

df4290d (Nov 13) was built on an older copy and silently undid earlier work.
Restored, while keeping its intended changes (four approved layouts, phonetic
typing, hidden empty suggestion bar, tighter on-screen keyboard):
- Word-style grouped ribbon, Liquid Glass chrome, Tools → law dictionary
- layout files: OpenBangla .json, Keyman .kmx/.kmp, Keyman rule typing
- hidden-layout lists; a chosen custom layout survives reload
- CSP <meta> in the production build (missing since charset became "UTF-8");
  the build now stops if it cannot add it
- index.html robots/description/status-bar meta; popovers in <body>
- Keyman test-file licences, decision 60, precomposed য় in FontPicker
- browser tests before deploy
Tests: skip v8 golden cases for layouts the app no longer offers; align the
logo, layout-list and suggestion-bar tests; harden one flaky test; one retry on CI.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01T69dVbubfB9R2bUgWo6BZy
